RUN TEST SUMMARY
================================================================================

Quick Test Commands:
  # Run all scenarios (normal + resume modes)
  ./compare_resume_perf.sh

  # Run with tables disabled
  ./compare_resume_perf.sh --no-tables

  # Custom: 10K nodes, 2s time chunks, SLIM format
  ./compare_resume_perf.sh custom SEGMENT 10000 0 2000 true true true

  # Custom: 10K nodes, normal mode (no chunking)
  ./compare_resume_perf.sh custom SEGMENT 10000 0 0 false false false

Options:
  --tables      : Enable table display (default)
  --no-tables   : Disable all table output for cleaner logs

Parameter Guide:
  STORE         : SEGMENT | DOCUMENT
  NODES         : Number of test nodes (e.g., 10000, 20000)
  CHUNK_SIZE    : Nodes per chunk (0=disabled)
  CHUNK_TIME_MS : Milliseconds per chunk (0=disabled, 1000=1s)
  RESUME        : true | false (enable resume indexing)
  PT_TRAVERSAL  : true | false (PathTree traversal optimization)
  SLIM_FORMAT   : true | false (frontier-based minimal storage)

Key Metrics Explained:
  Time(s)       : Total indexing time
  Throughput    : Nodes indexed per second
  Verified      : Count of successfully indexed documents (uses keyset pagination)
  Runs          : Number of chunks/cycles
  PTTrav        : PathTree traversal enabled (Y/N)

Performance Tips:
  ✓ SLIM format is 3x faster than NORMAL mode for large indexes
  ✓ Time-based chunking (1000ms) provides optimal balance
  ✓ PathTree reduces SegmentStore reads by 95-99%
  ✓ Incremental searchability: content visible after each chunk

Output Files:
  perf_resume_results.txt     : Complete test output with all metrics
  perf_resume_summary.txt     : Performance comparison table
  SEGMENT_*_*.out             : Individual scenario outputs

Common Scenarios:
  NORMAL mode                 : Traditional one-shot indexing
  RESUME + Full PathTree      : Resumable with full state (larger storage)
  RESUME + SLIM PathTree      : Resumable with minimal state (FASTEST!)

